@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "phone.zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk User Phone Number Integration
	Testing user phone number sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB and web.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | phone.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Phone                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                             |
	* I update the web password for user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "testtest"
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Phone Automotive |
	| Code         | PHONEAUTO        |
	| Type         | Group            |
	| Industry     | Automotive       |
	| Tier         | Premier          |
	| Max Contacts | 10               |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street  |
	| Country      | United States    |
	| State        | California       |
	| City         | Diamond Bar      |
	| Zip          | 91765            |
	| Region       | US               |
	| Language     | English          |
	* I assign a user the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "PHONEAUTO"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "PHONEAUTO"
	Then the organization "Phone Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present via the external id search api on zendesk.liferay.com
	* I wait for "2" minutes

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	* I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number | |
	* I log out of the web homepage
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Phone Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following screen names from web.liferay.com
	| phone.customer1 |
	* I tear down the users with the following screen names from customer.liferay.com
	| phone.customer1 |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PHONEAUTO |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Phone Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View user phone number update
	OSB user phone number updates to details on web should sync properly to Zendesk.

	Given I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	And I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number  | +15558402834 |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the phone number "+15558402834"
	When I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	And I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number | 5559873461 |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the phone number "+15558402834"
	When I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	And I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number | +15554394671 |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the phone number "+15554394671"

Scenario: View user phone number delete
	OSB user phone number deletions to details on web should sync properly to Zendesk.

	Given I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	And I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number  | +15558402834 |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the phone number "+15558402834"
	When I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	And I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number | |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should not have the phone number "+15558402834"

Scenario: View user phone number with no country code update
	OSB user phone numbers with no country code updates to details on web should not sync to Zendesk.

	Given I log into the web homepage as "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "testtest"
	And I update my phone number as "phone.customer1" to the following values
	| Number  | 5558402834 |
	And I log out of the web homepage
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "phone.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should not have the phone number "5558402834"

Scenario: View user phone number from no country code to country code update
	OSB user phone numbers that go from no country code to country code on web should sync to Zendesk.

